1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:08,560
Before using X-Tool Metal Fab Laser Welder, please carefully watch this video and read the safety instructions for the product.

2
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:14,560
Strictly follow all the safety instructions and regulations. Safety is our top priority.

3
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:25,560
Always ensure you are wearing the proper protective equipment, such as laser safety goggles that protect your eyes from laser beams at the wavelength of around 1080 nanometers.

4
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:30,560
Always use the product in a laser-controlled area with laser safety barriers.

5
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:39,560
Ensure that everyone entering the laser-controlled area has been trained in laser safety and warn all the necessary personal protective equipment.

6
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:42,560
1. How a laser beam travels

7
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:47,560
Now, let's begin with understanding how a laser beam travels.

8
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:50,560
The welding head emits two types of laser beams.

9
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:58,560
One is a visible red beam used for positioning, and the other is an invisible high-power infrared beam used for processing.

10
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:04,560
The infrared laser beam will diverge from the focal point and create a cone of radiation.

11
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:09,560
As the beam moves away from the focal point, its power density decreases.

12
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:17,560
Even though the laser power is weakened as the beam gets farther from the welding head, it can still be high enough to cause harm to skin and eyes.

13
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:23,560
Keep people away from the laser reflection zone. Never look into the laser outlet.

14
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:27,560
2. Important safety measures

15
00:01:27,560 --> 00:01:33,560
Everyone inside the laser-controlled area should wear the following protective equipment.

16
00:01:33,560 --> 00:01:43,560
Laser safety goggles or face shield certified to protect against laser radiation of around 1080 nanometers with an optical density greater than 6.

17
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:48,560
Laser and heat-resistant clothing and gloves and a dust mask.

18
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:53,560
Never look directly into the laser outlet or point the outlet at any body part.

19
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:59,560
Ensure that a fire extinguisher and other safety equipment are available in the laser processing area.

20
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:04,560
Do not place flammable or combustible materials in the laser processing area.

21
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:09,560
Never process containers with flammable or combustible materials.

22
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:13,560
3. Key components and controls of the welder

23
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:18,560
Now, let's walk through the key components and controls of the laser welder.

24
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:24,560
Emergency stop button. In case of any exception, press the button to immediately shut off the machine.

25
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:33,240
To restart the machine, rotate and pull out the button.

26
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:39,240
USB key, insert the USB key to enable the laser processing function.

27
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:43,240
The USB key can also be used to establish an interlocked entrance.

28
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:48,240
For more details, refer to the tutorials on supportxtool.com.

29
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:51,240
Shielding gas supply.

30
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:54,240
Laser processing uses shielding gas.

31
00:02:54,240 --> 00:03:01,240
Keep the gas cylinders away from the processing area and out of the path of any laser reflections.

32
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:06,240
Workpiece sensing cable. Connect the workpiece sensing cable to port 4.

33
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:11,240
Then, clamp its other end to the workpiece or the conductive work table.

34
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:16,540
Do not clamp it to the welding head.

35
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:24,540
4. Welding operations. On the touchscreen, activate both the enable lasering and enable wire feeding functions.

36
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:28,540
Ensure the welding head is in contact with the workpiece.

37
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:32,540
Press the grip sensing button and the welding head indicator will flash green,

38
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:36,540
indicating the machine is ready to emit laser.

39
00:03:36,540 --> 00:03:39,540
Press the firing trigger to start laser welding.

40
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:46,540
During laser welding, do not hold the workpieces in your hand or place your hand under the workpieces,

41
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:49,540
as the heat generated by welding can burn the skin.

42
00:03:49,540 --> 00:03:53,540
Laser beams can reflect from multiple surfaces.

43
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:58,540
Diffuse reflection from rough surfaces can spread over a large area.

44
00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:02,540
Always stay alert to the danger of laser radiation during welding.

45
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:05,540
Only observe the weld pool from behind the welding head.

46
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:08,540
Do not choose any other position for observation.

47
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:14,540
If anyone stands in the laser reflection zone, stop laser emission immediately.

48
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:19,540
If the metal fails to melt completely, the laser beam may diffuse from the welding spot.

49
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:23,540
Stop processing immediately to avoid laser hazards.

50
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:26,540
Always remain vigilant during laser processing.

51
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:31,540
If you find any potential risks, stop laser emission immediately.

52
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:36,540
The smoke generated during welding may contain toxic particles.

53
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:40,540
It is recommended to use an exhaust system to remove the smoke.

54
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:44,540
Operators must also wear necessary respiratory protective equipment.

55
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:47,540
5. Stop processing.

56
00:04:47,540 --> 00:04:53,540
To pause the machine, deactivate the enable wire feeding and enable lasering functions.

57
00:04:53,540 --> 00:04:58,540
If you have finished processing, turn off the machine's power and gas supply.

58
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:05,540
Following these steps and adhering to the safety instructions can help promote a smooth and safe welding experience.

59
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:07,540
Thank you for watching.
